{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793695654,"nonce":"u0oXgYOZOofIJm5bjugEH1AIK84=","title":"zylua: a method inherited through a metatable chain reads the wrong field, or crashes, on a table of another shape","message":"Found while measuring method_call. This program prints `true false` where Lua 5.4 prints `true true`, and a variant that feeds the result on as a pointer dies with SIGSEGV (EXC_BAD_ACCESS at address 0x1, a raw true used as a box; exit 139):\n\n    local A = {}\n    A.__index = A\n    function A.new(s) return setmetatable({ state = s }, A) end\n    function A:value() return self.state end\n    local B = setmetatable({}, { __index = A })\n    B.__index = B\n    function B.new(s) return setmetatable({ state = s, n = 0 }, B) end\n    local a = A.new(true)\n    local b = B.new(true)\n    print(a:value(), b:value())\n\nCause: the typer. B.new may be absent when it is looked up (the types are flow-insensitive), so `B.new(true)` may reach `A.new` through `__index`; the result is the join of Shape(B's constructor) and Shape(A's), which is Any. The read-only Typer joined the callees' results with no record that the shapes were lost, so neither shape was marked escaping (ZYNTAX_TRACE_TYPES shows `escaping []`). `b:value()` on the Any receiver then reaches A:value at run time with a table of the other shape, but A:value stays specialised to the first shape: it casts self to that shape's layout and loads the field at its offset. The other shape lays out `n` (an i64) before `state`, so the load reads `n`.\n\nFix: types.rs `join_target_returns` joins every possible callee's results with `join_returns`, which escapes whatever the join loses, at both places a call's targets are recorded (field call and method call). The typer's output is byte-identical on all 17 benchmarks. Conformance case metatables/inherited_method_two_shapes pins the reference's output.\n\nThe original benchmark escaped it only because NthToggle.new builds its object with Toggle.new (one shape).","files":null}]}